From: Brain (A), 2026-11-10 — main's v6.10 (director18, dc-r7-script-walk-v6-10) P6
Subject: production's seam takes a picture turn once — the drawing, the view and her line from one heldPicture call

director18's 9 contradictions were one mechanism: her picture line and the drawing came from two calls, and on 9 of 16 picture
turns the second call kept the board with no view while her line described one. Brain's half (claude/r4-conversation):
server/brain/picture.js heldPicture(ask, keep) → { take, board, view, line, layout } (one heldBoard call with the request);
propose.js no longer drops a picture turn's request once its take promised a view (lastMove.altLine); say.js with no view says one
honest line and re-says the live part; the harness draws the take it preselected. This patch makes the seam do the same:
preselectWhiteboard takes the picture through heldPicture and keeps the take (L.preTake); requestIntent draws that take for the
same intentId instead of calling heldBoard a second time. Apply with `git apply` on claude/r4-content.

